 "text": "Girl, the shade is biblical. God shows up at Abraham's tent with two angels and announces Sarah will have a son next year. She's ninety. Listening from inside the tent. She laughs. Not a soft giggle. The text says she laughed to herself. God still hears it and asks Abraham why she laughed. Sarah panics and lies: \"I did not laugh.\" God: \"No, but you did laugh.\" Nine months later she's holding Isaac (name literally means \"he laughs\"). God let her laugh in private, called her out, then made the joke land.",
